","charityNumber":"202918","addressCountry":"United Kingdom","addressLocality":"Oxford"}]},"publisher":{"self":"https://api.threesixtygiving.org/api/v1/org/GB-GOR-D2/","org_id":"GB-GOR-D2"},"data_license":{"url":"http://www.nationalarchives.gov.uk/doc/open-government-licence/version/3/","name":"Open Government Licence 3.0 (United Kingdom)"}},{"grant_id":"360G-CR-1658712","data":{"id":"360G-CR-1658712","title":"Repair and Rehabilitation of WASH Facilities in Households in Jordan","currency":"GBP","awardDate":"2015-09-30T00:00:00+00:00","description":"Syrian Refugees have been fleeing the devastating impact of the Syrian Civil War since 2011, however with the increase in reporting and border closures the impact of the mass migration is being felt throughout Europe and neighbouring Countries. Oxfam have identified the needs of Syrian refugees fleeing to Jordan and have designed a water, sanitation and hygiene (WASH) project to support these needs. This includes supporting Syrian refugees and vulnerable Jordanian households with WASH support in the form of repairs and rehabilitation.","dateModified":"2022-02-24T00:00:00+00:00","plannedDates":[{"endDate":"2017-02-14T00:00:00+00:00","duration":12,"startDate":"2016-01-01T00:00:00+00:00"}],"amountAwarded":300000,"beneficiaryLocation":[{"name":"Jordan","countryCode":"JO"}],"fundingOrganization":[{"id":"GB-CHC-326568","name":"Comic Relief"}],"recipientOrganization":[{"id":"GB-COH-00612172","name":"Oxfam GB","location":[{"countryCode":"GB"}],"charityNumber":"202918.0","companyNumber":"612172.0","addressCountry":"United Kingdom"}]},"publisher":{"self":"https://api.threesixtygiving.org/api/v1/org/GB-CHC-326568/","org_id":"GB-CHC-326568"},"data_license":{"url":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/","name":"Creative Commons Attribution 4.0 International (CC BY 4.0)"}},{"grant_id":"360G-CR-1873680","data":{"id":"360G-CR-1873680","title":"Combating Sexual and Gender-Based Violence to retain girls and boys in Malawian schools for improved","currency":"GBP","awardDate":"2016-07-13T00:00:00+00:00","description":"This project aims to tackle the prevalence of School Based Sexual Violence in schools. It will work with pupils, schools staff and communities to raise awareness and build effective and functional mechanisms to report and deal with any. There will be a primary focus on girls but boys are clearly integral to this work through their involvement and the ability and relevance of the mechanisms to support any incidences of sexual abuse against boys and young men. The mechanisms created will ensure that both communities and schools remain safe places for young people to grow up and develop in. Working with two experienced local organisations, Oxfam Malawi will be part of an effective partnership.","dateModified":"2022-02-24T00:00:00+00:00","plannedDates":[{"endDate":"2020-03-27T00:00:00+00:00","duration":36,"startDate":"2016-08-01T00:00:00+00:00"}],"amountAwarded":1000000,"beneficiaryLocation":[{"name":"Malawi","countryCode":"MW"}],"fundingOrganization":[{"id":"GB-CHC-326568","name":"Comic Relief"}],"recipientOrganization":[{"id":"GB-COH-00612172","name":"Oxfam GB","location":[{"countryCode":"GB"}],"charityNumber":"202918.0","companyNumber":"612172.0","addressCountry":"United Kingdom"}]},"publisher":{"self":"https://api.threesixtygiving.org/api/v1/org/GB-CHC-326568/","org_id":"GB-CHC-326568"},"data_license":{"url":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/","name":"Creative Commons Attribution 4.0 International (CC BY 4.0)"}},{"grant_id":"360G-CR-2587897","data":{"id":"360G-CR-2587897","title":"QuidsIn","currency":"GBP","awardDate":"2017-03-15T00:00:00+00:00","description":"QuidsIn is a digital payment card for people on low incomes that incorporates an emergency savings fund. Users have a prepayment card that is used for everyday shopping. Members save small amounts as they shop and this saving is matched by corporate/statutory partners. Members redeem their savings when they experience financial shock.","dateModified":"2022-05-30T00:00:00+00:00","plannedDates":[{"endDate":"2017-10-11T00:00:00+00:00","duration":4,"startDate":"2017-04-01T00:00:00+00:00"}],"amountAwarded":41010,"grantProgramme":[{"title":"Tech for Good Legacy"}],"beneficiaryLocation":[{"name":"United Kingdom","geoCode":"K02000001","countryCode":"GB","geoCodeType":"CTRY"}],"fundingOrganization":[{"id":"GB-CHC-326568","name":"Comic Relief"}],"recipientOrganization":[{"id":"GB-CHC-202918","name":"Oxfam GB","location":[{"name":"England","geoCode":"E92000001","geoCodeType":"CTRY"},{"name":"South East","geoCode":"E12000008","geoCodeType":"RGN/GOR"},{"name":"Oxford","geoCode":"E07000178","geoCodeType":"LAD"}],"charityNumber":"202918.0","companyNumber":"612172.0"}]},"publisher":{"self":"https://api.threesixtygiving.org/api/v1/org/GB-CHC-326568/","org_id":"GB-CHC-326568"},"data_license":{"url":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/","name":"Creative Commons Attribution 4.0 International (CC BY 4.0)"}},{"grant_id":"360G-EFF-11-3220","data":{"id":"360G-EFF-11-3220","title":"TASK to Oxfam UK","currency":"GBP","awardDate":"2011-12-20T00:00:00.000Z","description":"Towards Project costs A contribution towards the East African Appeal.","dateModified":"2020-10-05T12:16:31.000Z","plannedDates":[{"duration":12}],"amountAwarded":2000.0,"grantProgramme":[{"title":"TASK by Trustee"}],"classifications":[{"title":"Social Change"},{"title":"poverty relief"},{"title":"Beneficiary / All"}],"beneficiaryLocation":[{"name":"Overseas (Ex UK)"}],"fundingOrganization":[{"id":"GB-CHC-200051","name":"Esmée Fairbairn Foundation"}],"recipientOrganization":[{"id":"GB-CHC-202918","url":"http://www.oxfam.org.uk","name":"Oxfam UK","postalCode":"OX4 2JY","charityNumber":"202918"}]},"publisher":{"self":"https://api.threesixtygiving.org/api/v1/org/GB-CHC-200051/","org_id":"GB-CHC-200051"},"data_license":{"url":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/","name":"Creative Commons Attribution 4.0 International (CC 